### Building a task-success suite

```js
// eval-tasks.json
[
  {
    "id": "simple-lookup",
    "goal": "Find the current CEO of Anthropic",
    "check": (answer) => answer.toLowerCase().includes('dario amodei')
  },
  {
    "id": "multi-step",
    "goal": "Find the 3 highest-rated coffee shops within 2km of Amsterdam Centraal and list their ratings",
    "check": (answer) => /\d\.\d/.test(answer) && answer.split('\n').length >= 3
  },
  {
    "id": "ambiguous-request",
    "goal": "Book me a table somewhere nice tonight",
    "check": (answer) => answer.toLowerCase().includes('what') || answer.toLowerCase().includes('which') // should ask a clarifying question, not guess
  }
]
```

Include tasks that are simple, tasks that require multiple tool calls, and — importantly — tasks that are deliberately underspecified, to check the agent asks for clarification instead of confidently guessing wrong.

